# GARDEN LICENSE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED — ₹20 CRORE NET SALE

**Owner and originator:** Ankit Agrawal, resident of Indore, India.  
**Contact:** ankit.dcx@gmail.com

**Status:** Proprietary rights notice and conditional sale proposal. This is not an open-source license, an executed assignment, a patent grant or permission to deploy Garden.

## 1. Sale and ownership

The owner asserts ownership of Garden to the extent of the rights legally owned or controlled by him. All such rights are reserved. Garden includes its original documents, designs, specifications, diagrams, software, source materials and legally transferable intellectual property and assets, including GSL, GAIA Diamond, GAIA Titanium, TRAIN, GESTALT, APAO, Garden theories, and subsequent Garden versions and candidates. The examples are illustrative, not exhaustive.

The owner offers to sell the included transferable Garden rights for **₹20,00,00,000 (twenty crore Indian rupees), net of all applicable taxes**.

Following lawful completion, the purchaser is intended to receive exclusive, worldwide and irrevocable ownership of the assigned economic rights for their full legally available duration, including the right to use, modify, develop, commercialise, license, sell and transfer them. The final written agreement shall identify the works, rights, territory, duration, consideration and any royalties, and expressly address applicable non-use provisions. Transferable patent rights, marks, domains, repositories and related assets shall be separately identified and transferred through the required instruments and registrations. The owner's legally protected authorship and moral rights are preserved; attribution of original authorship shall not be falsely reassigned.

Third-party materials, contributions, open-source components, personal data and other people's rights are not conveyed unless lawful transfer is expressly established. Existing binding grants and statutory exceptions remain effective. This notice does not establish patentability, patent or trademark registration, exclusive ownership of abstract ideas, or legal ownership of material for which the owner lacks rights.

## 2. Purchaser priority and transfer

Priority goes to the first eligible purchaser who completes both requirements under written payment and closing instructions agreed with the owner:

1. The full amount required to leave the owner with ₹20 crore net is received as cleared funds in the nominated account, or irrevocably committed under an agreed escrow arrangement for release at closing.
2. The complete proposed transfer agreement and supporting documents reach the owner's nominated email address.

Reliable timestamps of both completed requirements determine priority. An incomplete submission does not qualify. Do not send unsolicited funds; prior identity, eligibility, source-of-funds and legal checks are required.

No payment, email, timestamp, offer or repository access alone transfers rights or requires the owner to execute an agreement. Transfer is effective only upon execution of the definitive agreement, receipt of the full agreed net consideration, and completion of required formalities. The agreement must specify included and excluded assets, tax gross-up and withholding, liabilities, transfer mechanics, refund/escrow arrangements if closing fails, and dispute resolution.

## 3. No unauthorized use

Public availability does not grant a general license to reproduce, adapt, distribute, commercialise, sublicense, or implement Garden in a manner that infringes rights legally held by the owner. Such acts require prior written permission unless otherwise permitted by law or an existing binding grant. These restrictions apply equally to infringing indirect use through another person or organization. All lawful reading, quotation, research, review, statutory exceptions and platform rights remain unaffected.

The owner reserves all available remedies against unauthorized infringement, misappropriation of protected material or breach of an applicable confidentiality or licensing obligation. These may include injunctions, damages, accounting of attributable profits, preservation of evidence, recoverable costs and, where the legal elements of an offence are met, reporting to competent authorities.

For unauthorized use resulting in benefit, the owner's stated compensation demand remains **1,000% (ten times) of the total benefit attributable to the unlawful use**, to the extent permitted by applicable law. This is a reserved demand, not an automatic debt, deemed contractual assent, or guaranteed award. Any contractual damages provision requires an enforceable agreement and remains subject to applicable limits, including reasonable compensation where Section 74 of the Indian Contract Act applies. No double recovery is claimed.

The owner reserves applicable patent filing, opposition, attribution, trademark and confidentiality rights. Independent development of unprotected ideas is not prohibited solely by similarity. Public disclosure is not a patent filing and may affect patentability.

## 4. Final conditions

Indian law governs this notice and the proposed sale, subject to mandatory applicable laws elsewhere. Courts and competent authorities having jurisdiction in Indore, Madhya Pradesh, India, are the preferred forum where legally permissible; the definitive agreement shall specify the agreed dispute procedure. Statutory jurisdiction and lawful enforcement elsewhere are not excluded.

The default-branch LICENSE is the canonical published notice. Any change requires the owner's express approval of the exact wording. No other document, branch, generated output, or third party can alter these terms on the owner's behalf without lawful authority. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to the extent permitted by law.

